      "math_academy_id": "e-13375",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{1}{64}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the numbers $1$ and $64$ are both perfect cubes. \n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{1}{64}},$ we express $\\dfrac{1}{64}$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{64}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{4}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1\\cdot 1\\cdot 1}{4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
